    "title": "What the commemoration of the 235th anniversary of Bois Caïman means for Haiti’s memory and future",
    "deck": "August 14, 1791, put in motion the first major anti-slavery movement in Haiti — part Vodou ceremony, part political congress, and wholly a movement of protest and resistance.",
    "source": "Global Voices",
    "sourceId": "global-voices",
    "sourceUrl": "https://globalvoices.org/2026/09/13/what-the-commemoration-of-the-235th-anniversary-of-bois-caiman-means-for-haitis-memory-and-future/",
